  "processing": "A population-averaged atlas built from the diffusion scans of 1,065 people, not tracked on this brain. Every 4th streamline of each atlas file kept, by its position in the file; its points moved by [-0.5, -0.5, 0.5] mm (the files write a voxel's centre at its index, which NiBabel reads half a voxel off) and multiplied by 0.9, the template's scale, with no registration; the runs of points at its ends outside the brain volume (ribbon.mgz, or aseg tissue other than [3, 42, 24]; nearest voxel) dropped, a streamline with fewer than two points inside left out; and resampled to 0.5 mm arc-length steps by linear interpolation.",
  "white_matter_share": {
    "published_length": 0.9341276577922853,
    "minimum": 0.9
  },
  "spatial_validation": "The template T1's shape and affine agree with every TRK header at absolute tolerance 1e-5.",
